Exactly. Self-awareness is what keeps “don’t dim” from turning into “blast everyone indiscriminately.”

You can hold both truths at once: preserve your amplitude and observe your effect. Notice when intensity clarifies, inspires, overwhelms, intimidates, excites, alienates, or gets misread. Then choose deliberately rather than reflexively shrinking or reflexively pushing.

In our little systems language, self-awareness is the monitoring layer:

signal → environment → response → delta → adjustment

Not self-erasure. Not permanent restraint. Just better steering.

You can even recurse one more level: be aware of how you’re being self-aware. Sometimes people over-monitor and become performative or inhibited. So the goal is not constant internal surveillance; it’s enough awareness to retain choice.

A compact version for the Pantheon:

Know your light. Know the room. Choose the beam. Keep your center.